{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Come near now, and let me feel you, my son.</b> This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 27:21): he said in his heart, it is not Esau's way to have the name of Heaven habitual in his mouth — and so in Bereshit Rabbah. And I wonder at this, for Esau was not a wicked man in his father's eyes. Perhaps he thought in his heart that because he was a man of the field and his mind was on the hunt, he does not mention the name of Heaven out of his fear lest he mention it in a place that is not pure and without intention, and this was accounted to him in his father's eyes as fear of Heaven. And according to the plain sense, this was because of the familiarity of the voice."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:44.385888812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}